      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Dignity is not a gift you earn by fighting a tide that has already decided to drown you; it is a fragile illusion you cling to because it is the only thing that keeps you from being completely erased. The only way to reclaim dignity is to stop trying to force the world to change its mind and instead accept that your struggle is the only reality that matters. You are not waiting for the tide to crush you; you are the water that is rising, and the only way to survive is to let the water wash over you without making a sound.",
